su name tlat kwon ob text "bu" as text "en" from text "wiktionary" to text "en_all_nopic_2026-08" by text "absolutive_case" with text "case used to indicate the patient or experiencer of a verb’s action. The absolutive case is used to mark the subject of an intransitive verb, as well as the object of a transitive verb (inasmuch as they are codified in the English nominative-accusative system). Some languages that employ the absolutive case include Abkhaz, Basque, Chechen, Dyirbal, Hindi, Inuktitut, Hiligaynon, and Yup'ik." at text "source-gloss" be text ya
